From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:53:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Cap unretired G16 Works per firmware lane at 64

The firmware reads up to 128 Works ahead on a lane. In the Dota 2 stalls
its read cursor sat exactly 128 Works past the oldest unretired Work.
Metal keeps at most 64 command buffers in flight per queue. Bound each
lane to 64 unretired Works, applied as the existing workqueue
backpressure, so the driver never approaches that window.
max_lane_works=0 removes the cap.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs    |  4 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
index 7cddceb6c5d4..85ac52adfa59 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ fn probe<'bound>(
             default: 1,
             description: "Compute Work ordering against other queues: 1 waits in the kernel and submits Works without firmware dependency items (as Metal); 0 encodes firmware dependency items (the earlier behaviour, which can stall the firmware under heavy compute bursts)",
         },
+        max_lane_works: u32 {
+            default: 64,
+            description: "Maximum unretired Works per firmware lane (render TA/3D and compute) before submissions back off; 0: unlimited. The firmware stops completing Works past a 128-Work window per lane, so keep this at 127 or less; Metal keeps at most 64 command buffers in flight per queue",
+        },
         perf_base: u32 {
             default: 0,
             description: "Debug: GPU performance controller base pstate (0: ADT value; 10 is the top state)",
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
index 75f4e54a099e..6103191403cd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
@@ -587,6 +587,24 @@ fn reserve_flight(
                 // a ring. Like the channel epochs above, never let the head
                 // run half a ring past an unretired flight on this lane, or
                 // that flight's ring check stays false and it never retires.
+                // The firmware reads up to 128 Works ahead on each lane. With
+                // more unretired Works than that on a lane it stops completing
+                // them (Dota 2 bursts: 127 in flight never stalled, 129 did).
+                // This applies to every lane (render TA and 3D as well as
+                // compute), so bound each well below the window, as Metal does
+                // with at most 64 command buffers in flight per queue.
+                let cap = crate::module_parameters::max_lane_works.value() as usize;
+                if cap != 0
+                    && self
+                        .flights
+                        .iter()
+                        .filter(|f| f.queues.iter().any(|&(pointers, _)| pointers == lane.pointers))
+                        .count()
+                        >= cap
+                {
+                    self.report_pressure(16, "workqueue");
+                    return Err(EBUSY);
+                }
                 let next = (lane.head + entries[stage]) % 0x500;
                 if self.flights.iter().any(|f| {
                     f.queues
